::JOUR_U05_L06_Q_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.ETH.02] Source: Multimedia Spirit Week Package. Project: A student media team is creating a multimedia package about Spirit Week for the school website. Package Parts: A short article, a 20-second recap video, a photo gallery, and a captioned quote card from the student council president. Team Conflict: The video editor wants fast music and quick cuts. The reporter wants slower pacing so the quote is clear. The photo editor wants the gallery first because the photos are strong. The web editor says the package needs a consistent tone, accurate captions, and a logical order for readers. Audience: Students, families, and staff who want a clear recap of the week. Collaboration Need: The team must compromise respectfully, maintain a cohesive package, use accurate visuals, and prepare publication-ready work. Question 1: Which compromise best protects the video and quote? {
~A. Use the fastest music during the quote so the video feels exciting.#Not correct. Choice A says 'Use the fastest music during the quote so the video feels exciting.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
=B. Use upbeat music during action shots but slow down and lower music during the quote.#Correct. Step 1: identify the workflow or collaboration skill named in the standard. Step 2: connect the answer to the embedded newsroom scenario. This answer works because it protects accuracy, supports respectful teamwork, manages time, maintains cohesion, or prepares publication-ready work.
~C. Delete the quote so no one has to adjust pacing.#Not correct. Choice C says 'Delete the quote so no one has to adjust pacing.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
~D. Ignore the reporter concern because video is more important than clarity.#Not correct. Choice D says 'Ignore the reporter concern because video is more important than clarity.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
}
::JOUR_U05_L06_Q_Q02::[MLA.JOUR.DIG.02] Source: Multimedia Spirit Week Package. Project: A student media team is creating a multimedia package about Spirit Week for the school website. Package Parts: A short article, a 20-second recap video, a photo gallery, and a captioned quote card from the student council president. Team Conflict: The video editor wants fast music and quick cuts. The reporter wants slower pacing so the quote is clear. The photo editor wants the gallery first because the photos are strong. The web editor says the package needs a consistent tone, accurate captions, and a logical order for readers. Audience: Students, families, and staff who want a clear recap of the week. Collaboration Need: The team must compromise respectfully, maintain a cohesive package, use accurate visuals, and prepare publication-ready work. Question 2: Which package order is most logical? {
~A. Put the gallery first only because the photo editor likes the photos.#Not correct. Choice A says 'Put the gallery first only because the photo editor likes the photos.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
~B. Start with the quote card before readers know the topic.#Not correct. Choice B says 'Start with the quote card before readers know the topic.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
~C. Use random order because all package parts are about Spirit Week.#Not correct. Choice C says 'Use random order because all package parts are about Spirit Week.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
=D. Article, video, photo gallery, then quote card gives context before motion, details, and highlighted voice.#Correct. Step 1: identify the workflow or collaboration skill named in the standard. Step 2: connect the answer to the embedded newsroom scenario. This answer works because it protects accuracy, supports respectful teamwork, manages time, maintains cohesion, or prepares publication-ready work.
}
